reward text Profession recipes at Friendly and Honored
why Forever's trade camps: their best recipes, the Minimule and the Pack Kodo need standing, not only Merchant's Favor.

# Azeroth Commerce Authority (2586, Alliance) and Durotar Supply and Logistics
# (2587, Horde): Forever's trade camps. Each side earns only its own camp's
# standing (Forever's faction table locks the other side's at the bottom).
# Built from Forever's quest pages (reputation per quest: Shipping Label
# 98247/98248 2000 once; Crate Return 93862 50; the 150 Craftsman's Writs
# 94004-94360, all daily, 45 at 75, 60 at 125 and 45 at 200; the four
# "A Sealed Crate" quests give no reputation, only Merchant's Favor), the
# pages' writ customers (43 of the 45 Journeyman writs and one Expert writ;
# the other Expert and Artisan customers are not in the data, the beta
# stopped at level 30), npcs.json for the camps, the drop data for the writ
# envelopes (Sealed Journeyman's Writ from 173 world mobs of level 11-31),
# and Forever's client item table for the rewards it gates by standing
# (Advertising License Application Honored, the tabards Exalted).
# The Merchant's Favor prices, the Revered Packmule Treat, the Exalted Pack
# Kodo and the scribes' items (Forged Delivery Receipt at Friendly, Forger's
# Quill at Honored) are vendor rules the item table does not hold: they
# follow several beta reports that agree. Polestar cannot count Merchant's
# Favor. Numbers are base reputation; the Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to
# 10%. Every quest here is level 60, so no level cut applies. The Legacy perk
# Performance Bonus raises Merchant's Favor from crates, not reputation.
# ASSUMED: Crate Return (93862) is handed to Marcy Baker or Dokimi from their
# window (Classic-style repeatable; Forever's data names no giver). In-game
# check: who takes the Notarized Shipping Container.
# ASSUMED: Journeyman writs keep paying 75 past Honored (Forever's quest data
# gives the writs no standing limit). In-game check: a Journeyman writ turned
# in at Honored or above.
#
# Waylaid Crates (the camp's Merchant's Favor): one bundle of the materials a crate
# lists fills it (Apprentice Textiles: 40 Linen Cloth or 20 Light Leather), and the
# sealed crate goes to Marcy Baker or Dokimi (A Sealed Crate 91899/91904, turned in
# from their window: players' recordings). Apprentice and Journeyman crates open from
# level 10, Expert from 20, Artisan from 35 (Forever's item table); a white crate pays
# 5, 10 or 15 Merchant's Favor by rank, a green one twice that. The steps walk one
# Apprentice Textiles crate as the example; every crate works the same way.

step Reach level 10
  tip Waylaid Crates and writs open from level 10.
  level 10

step Buy a Waylaid Crate: Apprentice Textiles
  tip Mobs drop crates from level 10 too; every crate fills the same way.
  auction 248684 x1

step Get 40 Linen Cloth
  tip Humanoids drop it, or the Auction House. 20 Light Leather fills this crate too.
  collect 2589 x40 nearest

step Fill the Waylaid Crate
  tip Right-clicking the crate turns it into a Sealed Apprentice Crate.
  use 248684 anywhere

step Start the Shipping Label quest · the label in your bags
  tip The first crate or writ comes with a Shipping Label.
  accept 98247 item 280179 only Alliance
  accept 98248 item 280180 only Horde

step Hand in the Shipping Label · Marcy Baker, Three Corners, Redridge
  tip It pays 2,000 reputation, two thirds of the way to Friendly.
  only Alliance
  zone Redridge Mountains
  turnin 98247

step Hand in the Shipping Label · Dokimi, outside the Crossroads, The Barrens
  tip It pays 2,000 reputation, two thirds of the way to Friendly.
  only Horde
  zone The Barrens
  turnin 98248

step Hand in the Sealed Apprentice Crate · Marcy Baker, Three Corners, Redridge
  tip Merchant's Favor and silver; crates give no reputation.
  only Alliance
  zone Redridge Mountains
  when has 248765
  turnin 91899 direct npc 256390

step Hand in the Sealed Apprentice Crate · Dokimi, outside the Crossroads, The Barrens
  tip Merchant's Favor and silver; crates give no reputation.
  only Horde
  zone The Barrens
  when has 248765
  turnin 91899 direct npc 256386

step Get a Sealed Journeyman's Writ
  tip Mobs of about level 11 to 31 drop them; the Auction House sells writs too.
  collect 262888 x1 anywhere

step Open the Sealed Journeyman's Writ
  tip Inside is one Craftsman's Writ for a crafted item.
  use 262888 anywhere

step Start the quest on your Craftsman's Writ
  tip Each writ once a day; as many different writs a day as you like.
  task "Right-click the Craftsman's Writ in your bags"

